    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Неплохо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Not bad.' In Russian, 'not bad' leads into 'not bad' in a very natural everyday phrasing. Then Maks replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Да?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Huh?' Notice the word order: 'yes' comes first, and 'yes' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Только это не мой паштет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Only this isn't my pâté.' Here 'only' sets up the idea, while 'pâté' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Как?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What?' You'll hear 'how' all the time in the show, here connected with 'how'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Та же консистенция.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Same texture.' The key word here means 'that', which Maks combines with 'consistency'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "И состав я подобрал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And I got the ingredients right.' Maks starts with 'roster' and pairs it with 'I' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Подождите.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Wait.' Notice the word order: 'wait' comes first, and 'wait' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Что входит в ваш паштет?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What goes into your pâté?' The question word for 'what' comes right at the start, followed directly by 'pâté'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Это секрет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is a secret.' The first content word means 'this', and 'secret' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Пойдём.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Let's go.' A compact expression built around 'let's go' and 'let's go'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Посмотрим.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Take a look.' In Russian, 'have a look' leads into 'have a look' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "maks",
      "t": "Хорошо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Good.' Maks starts with 'good' and pairs it with 'good' to make the point clear. Let's listen to the dialog one more time.",
